     "embed": {
      "$type": "app.bsky.embed.external",
      "external": {
       "description": "The company flagged two new incidents as “critical,” yet did not discover or disclose them until months later.",
       "thumb": {
        "$type": "blob",
        "ref": {
         "$link": "bafkreihwuvvzk462gxvijbgiyr3l35vsbab2sqik6m4gegxq5aqbbwh4ze"
        },
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
        "size": 276247
       },
       "title": "OpenAI discloses four more rogue AI incidents involving financial, medical, and government data | Fortune",
       "uri": "https://fortune.com/2026/10/16/openai-discloses-four-more-rogue-incidents-involving-financial-medical-and-government-data/"
      }
     },
     "langs": [
      "fr"
     ],
     "text": "Until we solve the alignment problem at its source, AI models will continue to optimize for the wrong goals, and increasingly impactful real-world consequences may occur, beyond the ones described here. This is a critical issue I discussed in my blogpost last month, which is cited in the article."
    },
